{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe evening here in Vienna is quite warm, and the air in the opera house was thick with the scent of perfume and smoke. We sat closer to the stage than before, which made the experience vivid, though perhaps less comfortable for my neck. The Kleins extended their stay just for this, and I confess their enthusiasm was contagious.\n\nLablache was Figaro; he has a lightness about him that is almost natural, not forced. Fodor as Susanna is exquisite, and Donzelli’s Count had a dignity that felt less like acting and more like memory. Dardanelli’s Countess was lovely, though I found myself thinking of how Mozart’s music holds the soul in tension, moving from the particular complaint to a universal resolution. It is a small mirror of the spirit’s journey.\n\nI am tired but happy. I hope you are well, and that the boys are behaving. I shall write again soon.\n\nYour loving husband,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795080326,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":206,"prompt_tokens":938,"total_tokens":1144,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-bc0uSMJPo2garf0iDce7OGZa9hAHMZwR","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":938,"prompt_ms":919.883,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9806855010660981,"prompt_per_second":1019.6948959813368,"predicted_n":206,"predicted_ms":4874.021,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.77571219512195,"predicted_per_second":42.059728507530025}}